        "pageimage": "Pulp_-_Common_People.JPG",
        "extract": "\"Common People\" is a song by English alternative rock band Pulp, released in May 1995 by Island Records as the lead single from their fifth studio album, Different Class (1995). It reached No. 2 on the UK Singles Chart, becoming a defining track of the Britpop movement as well as Pulp's signature song. In 2014, BBC Radio 6 Music listeners voted it their favourite Britpop song in an online poll. In a 2015 Rolling Stone readers' poll it was voted the greatest Britpop song.\nThe song is a critique of the wealthy wanting to be \"like common people\" – ascribing glamour to poverty. This phenomenon is referred to as slumming or \"class tourism\". The song...",
